# charge_me_up_scotty.lic
=begin
      author: Picko
        name: charge_me_up_scotty
        game: gemstone
        tags: wizard, charge item, 517, recharge, wand, orb gem
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.2
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Recharges spent wands and used magic items with Charge Item (517).
  Same idea as fizzfuse (one command does the whole job), and the orb/rub
  messaging follows Demandred's ;ucharge and the gswiki Charge Item (517) page.

  What it does:
    1. Survey: casts Elemental Detection (405) at every candidate to read its
       spell, charges, whether it's mage rechargeable/empowerable, and the most
       you can push it to. Nothing chargeable means no orb gem gets used. The
       results are remembered: a run within 24 hours of a check (or another run)
       reuses them instead of casting 405 again (--fresh to re-check anyway).
    2. Appraises any orb gems it hasn't appraised before at the nearest gem shop
       (values are remembered), so the most valuable gem becomes the first orb.
    3. If there's no grot t'kel potion in grotsack, buys one: the bank first
       (only if you carry under 5,000 silvers), then the nearest alchemist,
       then deposits what's left. Sorena's (Icemule) potions are one dose, so
       expect another trip each time a new orb is needed.
    4. Goes to the nearest Wizard Guild workshop (charging bonus) unless --here.
    5. Pours the potion on an orb gem and casts 517 at it to make a
       pulsating orb, then casts 517 at the orb until it's humming (ready).
       A poured gem is remembered, so if a run stops before the orb is made,
       the next one uses that gem first without pouring again.
    6. For each item: waits for enough mana to fill it in as few rubs as it can,
       then RUBs the orb with the item in the right hand. Re-preps the orb when
       it shrinks, makes a new orb when it implodes, and stops an item when it's
       full, greened, or has had charge_maxrubs rubs (every rub past the first
       couple raises the chance of greening it).
       An item stopped short by the orb's limit ("unable to add any more charges"
       before your max: a cheaper gem's orb caps what it can add) gets one more try
       on the next orb. If none is made before everything else is done, it lets
       the orb run out (up to 30 minutes, not re-prepped) and makes the next one.
    7. Spent wands come from bigshot's dead wand container and go back to the
       fresh wand container; magic items come from chargesack and go to
       chargedsack. Items that aren't mage rechargeable stay where they were.
    8. Goes back where you started and prints a report.

  Candidates:
    - wands in bigshot's dead_wand_container (UserVars.op, the active profile)
    - with --topoff, wands in the fresh_wand_container that aren't at your max
    - everything in chargesack (statues, quartz orbs, blue crystals, coins...)

  Settings:
    ;vars set orbgemsack=<container>      orb gems (required for charging)
    ;vars set grotsack=<container>        grot t'kel potion, bought if missing (default: orbgemsack)
    ;vars set charge_pour=false           gems are already poured; don't pour (default true)
    ;vars set chargesack=<container>      used magic items to recharge (optional)
    ;vars set chargedsack=<container>     recharged magic items (default: chargesack)
    ;vars set greensack=<container>       greened items (default: where they'd go anyway)
    ;vars set charge_maxrubs=<n>          most rubs per item per session (default 3)
    ;vars set charge_symbol=false         never use Symbol of Mana (default true: while waiting
                                          to rub, whenever it's off cooldown; it costs Voln
                                          favor, and one "not enough favor" stops it for the run)

  Usage:
    ;charge_me_up_scotty          survey, then charge everything that needs it
    ;charge_me_up_scotty check    survey only: 405 every candidate and report
    ;charge_me_up_scotty help     usage and current settings

  Options:
    --here       charge where you are: no gem shop or workshop trip (a potion
                 run still happens if you have none)
    --topoff     also top off fresh-container wands that are below your max
    --fresh      cast 405 at everything again instead of using the last check

  Game text verified in Picko's logs: the 405 output (2026-09-02, 2026-10-06,
  2026-10-20), the potion purchase and pour, and APPRAISE (2026-10-20). The orb
  and rub lines come from the wiki and ;ucharge and haven't been seen live yet;
  any response the script doesn't recognize is printed in full.
=end

require 'json'

module ChargeMeUpScotty
  # === config ====================================================================
  DEFAULT_MAX_RUBS = 3
  # Casts at the orb before giving up on getting it to "humming tones of enchantment"
  PREP_MAX         = 20
  # Never-empowered items cap at 40 (gswiki)
  ITEM_CAP         = 40
  # Wait for this share of max mana at most before a rub, so the orb isn't left
  # waiting on the last few points of regen
  RUB_MANA_SHARE   = 0.9
  WORKSHOP_TAG     = 'wizard guild workshop'
  # Withdrawn for a grot t'kel potion only if you carry less (2,000 at Sorena's, 2026-10-20)
  POTION_SILVER    = 5_000
  # How long a 405 result is trusted. Items that aren't chargeable never change, so
  # those are kept until the item's gone.
  SURVEY_TTL       = 24 * 60 * 60
  SURVEY_PRUNE     = 30 * 24 * 60 * 60
  # gswiki: an orb gem has to be worth at least 1,000
  ORB_GEM_FLOOR    = 1_000
  # A gem the shop won't quote ("not buying anything this valuable") sorts first
  TOO_VALUABLE     = 1_000_000

  # === game text =================================================================
  PREP_DONE   = /^Your spell(?:song)? is ready\.|^You already have a spell readied|^You can't think clearly enough|^You are concentrating too intently|^You are too injured|^But you don't have any mana|^You can't make that dextrous|^You do not know that spell|cough up some blood/
  CAST_RT     = /^Cast Roundtime \d+ Seconds?\./
  CAST_FAIL   = /^Cast at what\?|^You don't have a spell prepared!|^But you don't have any mana|^You can't think clearly|^Your magic fizzles|^I could not find|^What were you referring to/
  WAIT_REGEX  = /^(?:\.\.\.w|W)ait ([0-9]+) sec(?:onds?)?\.?$/

  # 405 (verified): 'You sense that the wand is a magic item that holds the spell "Hurl Boulder"
  # with 7 charges.' / '... with no charge.' then 'It is a mage rechargeable item.' and 'You
  # estimate you're skilled enough to push this item to a maximum of 26 charges in a single session.'
  # A mage empowerable item (verified 2026-10-20, a tooled platinum bracelet) instead says 'It is a
  # mage empowerable item.', 'You determine the platinum bracelet can hold an additional 169
  # charges.' and 'Given enough time, you feel as though you could push this item to 8 charges.'
  # Empowered items aren't held to the 40-charge cap (gswiki).
  DETECT_SPELL   = /holds the spell "([^"]+)" with (\d+|no) charges?/
  DETECT_MAGE    = /It is a mage (?:rechargeable|empowerable|empowered) item/
  DETECT_EMPOWER = /It is a mage (?:empowerable|empowered) item/
  DETECT_MAX     = /maximum of (\d+) charges? in a single session|could push this item to (\d+) charges?/
  DETECT_ROOM    = /can hold an additional (\d+) charges?/
  DETECT_WEAR    = /signs of wear|sessions?\b.*\bwear/
  # The wear line every healthy item gets; only anything else is worth showing
  WEAR_FINE      = /can take several more sessions/
  DETECT_SHOP    = /can be recharged to its original capacity by a merchant/

  # Verified 2026-10-20: "You pour your grot t'kel potion on your uncut emerald.  You carefully
  # work the liquid in until it is all absorbed." (Sorena's potion: "That was the last drop.")
  # The poured gem comes back with a NEW ID, so it's re-read from the hand afterwards.
  POUR_OK       = /absorbed/
  POUR_BAD      = /evaporat/
  # Verified 2026-10-20: 'The gemcutter Zirconia takes the pink sapphire and inspects it carefully
  # before saying, "I'll give you 1,837 silvers for it if you want to sell."'
  APPRAISE_VALUE = /give you ([\d,]+) silvers?/
  APPRAISE_HIGH  = /not buying anything this valuable/
  APPRAISE_DONE  = Regexp.union(APPRAISE_VALUE, APPRAISE_HIGH, /not quite my field|I only deal in|worthless|not interested|^I could not find|^What were you referring to|must be holding/)
  # Verified in Picko's logs: "You call upon a special blessing from Koar." / "You feel a surge
  # of mana flow through you." and, short on favor, "You strain to perform the symbol of mana but
  # you are unable to call forth enough power."
  SYMBOL_OK       = /surge of mana flow through you|special blessing from Koar/
  SYMBOL_NO_FAVOR = /unable to call forth enough power/
  SYMBOL_DONE     = Regexp.union(/surge of mana flow through you/, SYMBOL_NO_FAVOR, /^You can't|^You don't|^You are not|^What were you/)
  ORB_READY     = /humming tones of enchantment|already prepared for charging/
  ORB_GROW      = /It grows in size/
  ORB_SHRINK    = /pulsating orb shrinks somewhat|^The orb shrinks/
  ORB_GONE      = /implodes/

  RUB_OK        = /fingers of essence caress|You successfully add \d+ additional charges?/
  RUB_COUNT     = /You successfully add (\d+) additional charges?/
  RUB_NO_MANA   = /You do not have enough mana|You feel terribly drained/
  RUB_FULL      = /You are unable to add any more charges/
  RUB_NOT_READY = /isn't properly prepared for recharging/
  RUB_FLOWS     = /unable to properly channel the flows/
  RUB_GREEN     = /flares a sickening green/
  RUB_GONE      = /^What were you referring to|^I could not find what you were referring to/
  RUB_DONE      = Regexp.union(RUB_OK, RUB_NO_MANA, RUB_FULL, RUB_NOT_READY, RUB_FLOWS, RUB_GREEN, RUB_GONE, /suddenly disintegrates/)

  GET_DONE      = /^You (?:remove|get|grab|pull|take|pick up|carefully remove|retrieve)|^Get what\?|^I could not find|^What were you referring to|^You need a free hand|^You can't/
  PUT_DONE      = /^You (?:put|place|slip|tuck|add|drop|carefully place|gently place)|^I could not find|^What were you referring to|won't fit|^That is closed|too (?:full|heavy|large)/

  # === helpers ===================================================================
  def self.msg(text)
    respond "[charge_me_up_scotty] #{text}"
  end

  def self.setting(name)
    value = UserVars.send(name).to_s.strip
    value.empty? ? nil : value
  end

  def self.pour?
    UserVars.charge_pour.to_s !~ /\A(?:false|no|off|0)\z/i
  end

  def self.max_rubs
    value = UserVars.charge_maxrubs.to_s
    value =~ /\A\d+\z/ && value.to_i.positive? ? value.to_i : DEFAULT_MAX_RUBS
  end

  def self.op_setting(key, fallback)
    op = UserVars.op.is_a?(Hash) ? UserVars.op : {}
    value = op[key].to_s.strip
    value.empty? ? fallback : value
  end

  # GS4 style names, the way bigshot and ;vars hold them: "buck.bag", "mail sack", "my cloak",
  # "sack". The last word is the noun; every other word has to start a word of the item's
  # name ("buck" matches "juniper buckskin bag", like the game's own adjective matching).
  def self.matches?(obj, name)
    words = name.to_s.strip.sub(/\Amy\s+/i, '').split(/[\s.]+/)
    return false if words.empty?

    obj.noun.to_s.casecmp?(words.last) && words[0..-2].all? { |word| obj.name.to_s =~ /\b#{Regexp.escape(word)}/i }
  end

  def self.find_container(name)
    return nil if name.nil?

    GameObj.inv.find { |obj| matches?(obj, name) }
  end

  # "look in" forces a fresh listing; GameObj#contents alone can be stale (lockerstow.lic)
  def self.contents(container)
    fput "look in ##{container.id}"
    container.contents.to_a
  end

  def self.held?(id)
    [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].any? { |hand| hand.id.to_s == id.to_s }
  end

  def self.hand(side)
    side == 'left' ? GameObj.left_hand : GameObj.right_hand
  end

  def self.side_of(id)
    %w[right left].find { |side| hand(side).id.to_s == id.to_s }
  end

  # === memory between runs =======================================================
  # Kept in CharSettings as JSON strings (a stored hash comes back as a settings proxy):
  #   charge_survey      item id => last 405 result
  #   charge_gem_values  gem id => appraised value
  #   charge_poured      ids of gems that were poured but not yet made into an orb
  def self.recall(key, empty)
    value = JSON.parse(CharSettings[key].to_s)
    value.is_a?(empty.class) ? value : empty
  rescue StandardError
    empty
  end

  def self.remember(key, value)
    CharSettings[key] = JSON.generate(value)
  end

  def self.wait_for(seconds = 3)
    (seconds * 10).to_i.times {
      return true if yield
      sleep 0.1
    }
    yield
  end

  # Every line the script reads passes through here, so the orb's ambient shrink and
  # implode messages are seen even while we're waiting on mana or doing something else
  def self.scan(line)
    @orb_ready = false if line =~ ORB_SHRINK || line =~ ORB_GONE
  end

  def self.drain
    while (line = get?)
      scan(line)
    end
  end

  # put, not fput or dothistimeout: those can swallow the response line we need, and
  # dothistimeout clears the buffer, which would drop an ambient "shrinks somewhat"
  def self.collect(action, done, timeout = 6)
    drain
    lines = []
    put action
    end_time = Time.now.to_f + timeout
    loop do
      line = get?
      if line.nil?
        sleep 0.1
      else
        scan(line)
        lines << line
        if line =~ WAIT_REGEX
          sleep [Regexp.last_match(1).to_i - 0.5, 0.3].max
          put action
          end_time = Time.now.to_f + timeout
          next
        end
        break if line =~ done
      end
      break if Time.now.to_f > end_time
    end
    lines
  end

  # Any lines that trail a result (the charge count can follow the success line)
  def self.more_lines(seconds)
    lines = []
    end_time = Time.now.to_f + seconds
    while Time.now.to_f < end_time
      line = get?
      if line
        scan(line)
        lines << line
      else
        sleep 0.1
      end
    end
    lines
  end

  # symbol: true (rub waits only) also uses Symbol of Mana whenever it's off cooldown
  def self.wait_for_mana(amount, reason = nil, symbol: false)
    amount = [amount.to_i, maxmana].min
    drain
    return if checkmana >= amount

    msg "Waiting for #{amount} mana#{reason ? " #{reason}" : ''} (you have #{checkmana})."
    until checkmana >= amount
      drain
      symbol_of_mana if symbol && symbol_ready?
      sleep 0.5
    end
  end

  # Voln's Symbol of Mana costs favor (about 460: 678 -> 218 on Picko, per Picko-attack-fire).
  # Without enough favor the game says "You strain to perform the symbol of mana but you are
  # unable to call forth enough power." and no cooldown starts, so a cooldown check alone would
  # retry it forever (Picko-attack-fire did 839 times). One failure turns it off for the run;
  # favor only comes back from hunting. ;vars set charge_symbol=false to never spend favor.
  def self.symbol?
    UserVars.charge_symbol.to_s !~ /\A(?:false|no|off|0)\z/i
  end

  def self.symbol_ready?
    symbol? && !@symbol_off && Spell[9813].known? && !Effects::Cooldowns.active?('Symbol of Mana')
  end

  def self.symbol_of_mana
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    before = checkmana
    text = collect("symbol of mana", SYMBOL_DONE).join("\n")
    waitrt?
    if text =~ SYMBOL_NO_FAVOR
      @symbol_off = true
      msg "Not enough Voln favor for Symbol of Mana; not trying it again this run."
    elsif text =~ SYMBOL_OK
      wait_for(2) { checkmana > before }
      msg "Symbol of Mana: #{before} -> #{checkmana} mana."
    else
      # Unrecognized: don't keep spamming it
      @symbol_off = true
      msg "Symbol of Mana didn't work as expected; not trying it again this run. The game said:"
      text.lines.each { |line| respond "    #{line.chomp}" }
    end
  end

  def self.take(id, from)
    collect("get ##{id}", GET_DONE)
    return false unless wait_for { held?(id) }

    @held[id.to_s] = from
    true
  end

  def self.stash(id, into)
    collect("put ##{id} in ##{into.id}", PUT_DONE)
    return false unless wait_for { !held?(id) }

    @held.delete(id.to_s)
    true
  end

  # For something whose ID may have changed in hand (a poured gem)
  def self.stash_hand(side, into, old_id = nil)
    return true if side.nil? || hand(side).id.nil?

    collect("put #{side} in ##{into.id}", PUT_DONE)
    return false unless wait_for { hand(side).id.nil? }

    @held.delete(old_id.to_s) if old_id
    true
  end

  # The item has to be in the right hand to RUB the orb with it
  def self.in_right_hand(id)
    fput "swap" if GameObj.left_hand.id.to_s == id.to_s && GameObj.right_hand.id.nil?
    wait_for { GameObj.right_hand.id.to_s == id.to_s }
  end

  # Gates every cast on the spell's full cost, re-read live right before the CAST
  # (casting short overextends you). Orb casts after the first only cost 1 mana per
  # the wiki, but waiting for 517's listed 17 is the safe side of that.
  def self.cast_at(num, target, done)
    spell = Spell[num]
    wait_for_mana(spell.mana_cost, "for #{spell.name}")
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    unless checkprep == spell.name
      collect("release", /^You feel the magic|^You don't have a prepared spell/) unless checkprep == 'None'
      lines = collect("prepare #{num}", PREP_DONE)
      unless lines.any? { |line| line =~ /^Your spell(?:song)? is ready\./ }
        msg "Couldn't prepare #{spell.name}. The game said:"
        lines.each { |line| respond "    #{line}" }
        exit
      end
    end
    wait_for_mana(spell.mana_cost, "for #{spell.name}")
    lines = collect("cast at #{target}", Regexp.union(done, CAST_FAIL))
    waitcastrt?
    lines
  end

  # Mana per charge, estimated (gswiki): the spell's cost for an elemental spell,
  # twice that for a Sorcerer spell, three times for anything else, minus 1 per 5
  # ranks of Elemental Mana Control but never below the spell's own cost
  def self.per_charge(rec)
    spell = rec[:spell] && Spell[rec[:spell]]
    return nil if spell.nil? || spell.mana_cost.to_i <= 0

    base = spell.mana_cost.to_i
    multiplier = case spell.circle.to_i
                 when 4, 5, 9 then 1
                 when 7 then 2
                 else 3
                 end
    [base * multiplier - Skills.emc.to_i / 5, base].max
  end

  # Enough mana to fill the item in one rub if we can hold it, else most of our max
  def self.rub_mana(rec)
    cap = (maxmana * RUB_MANA_SHARE).floor
    per = per_charge(rec)
    return cap if per.nil?

    [[per * (rec[:target] - rec[:charges]), cap].min, per].max
  end

  # === survey ====================================================================
  def self.detect(rec)
    lines = cast_at(405, "##{rec[:id]}", CAST_RT)
    text = lines.join("\n")
    if text =~ DETECT_SPELL
      rec[:spell] = Regexp.last_match(1)
      rec[:charges] = Regexp.last_match(2) == 'no' ? 0 : Regexp.last_match(2).to_i
    end
    rec[:before] ||= rec[:charges]
    rec[:mage] = text =~ DETECT_MAGE ? true : false
    rec[:empowered] = text =~ DETECT_EMPOWER ? true : false
    rec[:merchant] = text =~ DETECT_SHOP ? true : false
    room = text[DETECT_ROOM, 1]
    cap = rec[:empowered] && room ? rec[:charges].to_i + room.to_i : ITEM_CAP
    most = (match = text.match(DETECT_MAX)) ? (match[1] || match[2]).to_i : cap
    rec[:target] = [most, cap].min
    rec[:wear] = lines.find { |line| line =~ DETECT_WEAR }
    rec[:raw] = lines if rec[:spell].nil? && !rec[:merchant]
    rec
  end

  def self.candidates
    dead  = find_container(op_setting('dead_wand_container', 'bag'))
    fresh = find_container(op_setting('fresh_wand_container', 'sack'))
    items = find_container(setting(:chargesack))
    charged = find_container(setting(:chargedsack)) || items
    sources = []
    sources << [dead, fresh, :wand] if dead && fresh
    sources << [fresh, fresh, :wand] if fresh && @topoff
    sources << [items, charged, :item] if items

    msg "Can't find bigshot's wand containers (#{op_setting('dead_wand_container', 'bag')} / #{op_setting('fresh_wand_container', 'sack')})." unless dead && fresh
    msg "Can't find your chargesack (#{setting(:chargesack)})." if setting(:chargesack) && items.nil?

    seen = {}
    sources.uniq { |src, _dst, _kind| src.id }.flat_map { |src, dst, kind|
      fput "open ##{src.id}"
      contents(src).select { |obj|
        next false if seen[obj.id]
        next false if kind == :wand && obj.name !~ /\bwand\b/i
        next false if obj.type.to_s =~ /gem/ || obj.name =~ /grot t'kel/i

        seen[obj.id] = true
      }.map { |obj| { id: obj.id, name: obj.name, src: src, dst: dst, kind: kind, rubs: 0 } }
    }
  end

  def self.status_for(rec)
    if !rec[:mage]
      rec[:merchant] ? :merchant : :not_rechargeable
    elsif rec[:charges] >= rec[:target]
      :at_max
    else
      :charge
    end
  end

  # The last 405 result for this item, if it's still good: same name, and under a day
  # old unless it said the item can't be charged (that never changes)
  def self.cached(rec)
    entry = @survey_cache[rec[:id].to_s]
    return nil unless entry.is_a?(Hash) && entry['name'] == rec[:name]
    return entry unless entry['mage']

    Time.now.to_i - entry['at'].to_i < SURVEY_TTL ? entry : nil
  end

  def self.apply_cached(rec, entry)
    %i[spell charges target mage empowered merchant wear].each { |key| rec[key] = entry[key.to_s] }
    rec[:charges] = rec[:charges].to_i
    rec[:target] = rec[:target].to_i
    rec[:before] = rec[:charges]
    rec[:cached] = true
  end

  def self.cache_record(rec)
    return if rec[:spell].nil? && rec[:mage].nil?

    @survey_cache[rec[:id].to_s] = {
      'name' => rec[:name], 'spell' => rec[:spell], 'charges' => rec[:charges], 'target' => rec[:target],
      'mage' => rec[:mage], 'empowered' => rec[:empowered], 'merchant' => rec[:merchant], 'wear' => rec[:wear],
      'at' => Time.now.to_i
    }
  end

  def self.save_survey
    cutoff = Time.now.to_i - SURVEY_PRUNE
    @survey_cache.delete_if { |_id, entry| !entry.is_a?(Hash) || entry['at'].to_i < cutoff }
    remember('charge_survey', @survey_cache)
  end

  def self.survey
    recs = candidates
    if recs.empty?
      msg "Nothing to check: no wands in your dead wand container#{setting(:chargesack) ? ' and nothing in your chargesack' : ''}."
      return []
    end

    reuse = @fresh ? [] : recs.select { |rec| (entry = cached(rec)) && apply_cached(rec, entry) }
    unless reuse.empty?
      msg "Using your last check for #{reuse.size} item#{reuse.size == 1 ? '' : 's'} (--fresh to cast 405 at them again)."
    end
    to_detect = recs - reuse
    msg "Checking #{to_detect.size} item#{to_detect.size == 1 ? '' : 's'} with Elemental Detection." unless to_detect.empty?
    to_detect.each do |rec|
      unless take(rec[:id], rec[:src])
        rec[:status] = :missing
        next
      end
      detect(rec)
      cache_record(rec)
      stash(rec[:id], rec[:src])
    end
    recs.each { |rec| rec[:status] ||= status_for(rec) }
    save_survey
    @records = recs
  end

  # === the orb ===================================================================
  def self.orb_ids
    GameObj.loot.to_a.select { |obj| obj.name =~ /pulsating orb/i }.map(&:id)
  end

  def self.orb_alive?
    @orb_id && orb_ids.include?(@orb_id)
  end

  def self.orb_gems
    contents(@gemsack).select { |obj| obj.type.to_s =~ /gem/ && !@bad_gems.include?(obj.id) }
  end

  def self.gem_value(gem)
    @gem_values[gem.id.to_s]
  end

  def self.poured?(gem)
    @poured.include?(gem.id.to_s)
  end

  # A gem that's already poured goes first (its potion is spent), then the most valuable
  # (a pricier gem makes a longer-lasting orb), then any not appraised, in bag order.
  # Value varies a lot within one kind (uncut emeralds 3,517 and 7,612), so it's the
  # appraisal that counts, not the gem's name.
  def self.next_gem
    orb_gems.each_with_index.min_by { |gem, i| [poured?(gem) ? 0 : 1, -(gem_value(gem) || -1), i] }&.first
  end

  # APPRAISE every orb gem that hasn't been appraised before, at the nearest gem shop.
  # Values are remembered by gem, so this is a one-time stop per gem. It doesn't walk
  # back: the run goes on from here to the alchemist or workshop, and home at the end.
  def self.appraise_gems
    gems = orb_gems.reject { |gem| gem_value(gem) || poured?(gem) }
    return if gems.empty?

    msg "Appraising #{gems.size} orb gem#{gems.size == 1 ? '' : 's'} at the nearest gem shop so the best one is used first."
    go2('gemshop')
    unless Room.current&.tags.to_a.include?('gemshop')
      msg "Couldn't get to a gem shop; unappraised gems go in the order they're in your #{@gemsack.name}."
      return
    end

    gems.each do |gem|
      next unless take(gem.id, @gemsack)

      text = collect("appraise ##{gem.id}", APPRAISE_DONE).join("\n")
      if text =~ APPRAISE_VALUE
        @gem_values[gem.id.to_s] = Regexp.last_match(1).delete(',').to_i
      elsif text =~ APPRAISE_HIGH
        @gem_values[gem.id.to_s] = TOO_VALUABLE
      else
        msg "Couldn't get an appraisal for the #{gem.name}: #{text.lines.last.to_s.strip}"
      end
      stash(gem.id, @gemsack)
    end
    remember('charge_gem_values', @gem_values)

    ranked = orb_gems.select { |gem| gem_value(gem) }.sort_by { |gem| -gem_value(gem) }
    msg "Orb gems by value: #{ranked.map { |gem| "#{gem.name} #{gem_value(gem) >= TOO_VALUABLE ? '(too valuable to quote)' : gem_value(gem)}" }.join(', ')}."
    cheap = ranked.select { |gem| gem_value(gem) < ORB_GEM_FLOOR }
    msg "Under #{ORB_GEM_FLOOR} (an orb gem has to be worth at least that): #{cheap.map(&:name).join(', ')}. Those go last." unless cheap.empty?
  end

  # === grot t'kel potion =========================================================
  def self.go2(place)
    Script.run('go2', "#{place} --disable-confirm")
  end

  def self.find_potion
    contents(@grotsack).find { |obj| obj.name =~ /grot t'kel/i }
  end

  # Buys the first catalog item whose name matches pattern and returns it in hand, or nil
  # (summond's buy; the ORDER catalog is columns of "N. a name")
  def self.buy(pattern, what)
    number = nil
    Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("order", /Welcome to|catalog/i).each { |line|
      line.gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '').scan(/(\d+)\.\s+(.+?)(?=\s{2,}\d+\.|\s*\z)/) { |num, name| number ||= num if name =~ pattern }
    }
    if number.nil?
      msg "This shop doesn't sell #{what}."
      return nil
    end

    held = [GameObj.right_hand.id, GameObj.left_hand.id]
    fput "order #{number}"
    result = dothistimeout "buy", 5, /Sold for|hands you|need a free hand|enough|afford|What were you referring to/
    unless result =~ /Sold for|hands you/
      msg "Couldn't buy #{what}: #{result || 'no answer from the shop'}"
      return nil
    end

    item = nil
    wait_for { item = [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].find { |hand| hand.id && !held.include?(hand.id) } }
    item
  end

  # Bank (only if you carry less than POTION_SILVER), the nearest alchemist, then back
  # to where we were. Only called with empty hands and no live orb, so leaving is safe.
  def self.buy_potion
    msg "No grot t'kel potion in your #{@grotsack.name}. Buying one (bank if needed, then the alchemist)."
    return_room = Room.current&.id
    withdrew = false
    if Lich::Util.silver_count < POTION_SILVER
      go2('bank')
      line = dothistimeout "withdraw #{POTION_SILVER} silvers", 5, /hands you|don't have|not have|insufficient|only have/i
      unless line =~ /hands you/
        msg "Couldn't withdraw #{POTION_SILVER} silvers for a potion: #{line || 'no answer from the teller'}"
        go2(return_room) if return_room
        return nil
      end
      withdrew = true
    end

    go2('alchemist')
    potion = buy(/grot t'kel potion/, "a grot t'kel potion")
    if potion
      @held[potion.id.to_s] = @grotsack
      stash(potion.id, @grotsack)
    end
    if withdrew
      go2('bank')
      fput "deposit all"
    end
    go2(return_room) if return_room && Room.current&.id != return_room
    potion && find_potion
  end

  def self.ensure_potion
    find_potion || buy_potion
  end

  def self.pour_on(gem, potion)
    return false unless take(potion.id, @grotsack)

    lines = collect("pour ##{potion.id} on ##{gem.id}", Regexp.union(POUR_OK, POUR_BAD, /^You (?:can't|cannot)|^I could not find|^What were you/))
    lines += more_lines(1)
    # The last dose: "That was the last drop.  The grot t'kel potion shatters into twinkling dust."
    stash(potion.id, @grotsack) if held?(potion.id)
    return true if lines.any? { |line| line =~ POUR_OK }

    if lines.any? { |line| line =~ POUR_BAD }
      msg "#{gem.name} isn't an orb gem (the potion evaporated). Putting it back; take it out of your #{@gemsack.name}."
    else
      msg "Pouring the grot t'kel potion on #{gem.name} didn't work. The game said:"
      lines.each { |line| respond "    #{line}" }
    end
    @bad_gems << gem.id
    nil
  end

  # Pouring gives the gem a new ID (2026-10-20: casting at the old one got "Cast at what?"),
  # so read it back out of the hand it's in, carry its appraisal over, and remember it's
  # poured in case the run stops before the orb is made. Returns the gem as it is now.
  def self.after_pour(gem, side)
    wait_for(2) { hand(side).id && hand(side).id.to_s != gem.id.to_s }
    now = hand(side)
    if now.id.nil?
      msg "Lost track of the #{gem.name} after pouring on it. Stopping."
      return nil
    end
    if now.id.to_s != gem.id.to_s
      @held.delete(gem.id.to_s)
      @held[now.id.to_s] = @gemsack
      value = @gem_values.delete(gem.id.to_s)
      @gem_values[now.id.to_s] = value if value
      remember('charge_gem_values', @gem_values)
    end
    @poured << now.id.to_s unless @poured.include?(now.id.to_s)
    remember('charge_poured', @poured)
    now
  end

  # Turns the next orb gem into a pulsating orb on the ground. Hands must be empty.
  def self.make_orb
    loop do
      gem = next_gem
      if gem.nil?
        msg "Out of orb gems in your #{@gemsack.name}."
        return false
      end
      needs_pour = pour? && !poured?(gem)
      # Before the gem comes out: a potion run needs empty hands
      potion = needs_pour && ensure_potion
      if needs_pour && potion.nil?
        msg "No grot t'kel potion to pour on #{gem.name}. If your orb gems are already poured, ;vars set charge_pour=false"
        return false
      end
      return false unless take(gem.id, @gemsack)

      if needs_pour
        gem_side = side_of(gem.id)
        poured = pour_on(gem, potion)
        # By hand, not by ID: the pour may have swapped the gem's ID
        if poured.nil?
          stash_hand(gem_side, @gemsack, gem.id)
          next
        end
        unless poured
          stash_hand(gem_side, @gemsack, gem.id)
          return false
        end
        gem = after_pour(gem, gem_side)
        return false if gem.nil?
      end

      before = orb_ids
      msg "Making a pulsating orb from #{gem.name}#{gem_value(gem) ? " (#{gem_value(gem)})" : ''}."
      lines = cast_at(517, "##{gem.id}", CAST_RT)
      new_orb = nil
      wait_for { new_orb = (orb_ids - before).first }
      if new_orb
        @held.delete(gem.id.to_s)
        @poured.delete(gem.id.to_s)
        @gem_values.delete(gem.id.to_s)
        remember('charge_poured', @poured)
        remember('charge_gem_values', @gem_values)
        @orb_id = new_orb
        @orb_ready = false
        @gems_used += 1
        @orb_count += 1
        return true
      end

      msg "Casting 517 at #{gem.name} didn't make an orb. The game said:"
      lines.each { |line| respond "    #{line}" }
      stash(gem.id, @gemsack) if held?(gem.id)
      return false
    end
  end

  # Casts 517 at the orb until it's humming. Each cast can also shrink it.
  def self.prep_orb
    unknown = 0
    PREP_MAX.times do
      return false unless orb_alive?

      lines = cast_at(517, "##{@orb_id}", Regexp.union(ORB_READY, ORB_GROW, ORB_SHRINK, ORB_GONE, CAST_RT))
      if lines.any? { |line| line =~ ORB_READY }
        @orb_ready = true
        return true
      elsif lines.any? { |line| line =~ ORB_GONE }
        return false
      elsif lines.none? { |line| line =~ ORB_GROW || line =~ ORB_SHRINK }
        unknown += 1
        next if unknown < 3

        msg "The orb isn't responding the way it should. The game said:"
        lines.each { |line| respond "    #{line}" }
        return false
      end
    end
    msg "The orb still wasn't ready after #{PREP_MAX} casts."
    false
  end

  # An orb already in the room might be ours from an earlier run; one prep cast tells
  def self.adopt_orb
    orb_ids.each do |id|
      @orb_id = id
      lines = cast_at(517, "##{id}", Regexp.union(ORB_READY, ORB_GROW, ORB_SHRINK, ORB_GONE, CAST_RT))
      if lines.any? { |line| line =~ ORB_READY || line =~ ORB_GROW || line =~ ORB_SHRINK }
        msg "Using the pulsating orb that's already here."
        @orb_ready = lines.any? { |line| line =~ ORB_READY }
        @orb_count += 1
        return
      end
    end
    @orb_id = nil
  end

  def self.ensure_orb
    return true if orb_alive? && @orb_ready

    unless orb_alive?
      msg "The pulsating orb is gone." if @orb_id
      @orb_id = nil
      return false unless make_orb
    end
    prep_orb
  end

  # === charging ==================================================================
  # Returns :done, :orb_lost (item's back in its container, make a new orb and call
  # again), or :stop (no orb could be made)
  def self.charge(rec)
    return :stop unless ensure_orb

    # A retried item is wherever its last charge() left it
    home = rec[:loc] || rec[:src]
    return :done unless take(rec[:id], home) && in_right_hand(rec[:id])

    rec[:status] = :partial if %i[charge orb_limit].include?(rec[:status])
    short_on_mana = false
    while rec[:charges] < rec[:target] && rec[:rubs] < max_rubs
      unless orb_alive?
        stash(rec[:id], home)
        return :orb_lost
      end
      unless @orb_ready || prep_orb
        stash(rec[:id], home)
        return :orb_lost
      end

      wanted = short_on_mana ? (maxmana * RUB_MANA_SHARE).floor : rub_mana(rec)
      wait_for_mana(wanted, "to charge the #{rec[:name]}", symbol: true)
      next unless @orb_ready

      mana_before = checkmana
      lines = collect("rub ##{@orb_id}", RUB_DONE)
      lines += more_lines(1.5) if lines.any? { |line| line =~ RUB_OK }
      text = lines.join("\n")

      if text =~ RUB_GREEN
        rec[:rubs] += 1
        rec[:status] = :greened
        msg "The #{rec[:name]} flared green; it can't be recharged again."
        break
      elsif text =~ RUB_OK
        rec[:rubs] += 1
        short_on_mana = false
        if text =~ RUB_COUNT
          rec[:charges] += Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
        else
          detect(rec)
        end
        msg "#{rec[:name]}: #{rec[:charges]}/#{rec[:target]} charges after rub #{rec[:rubs]}."
      elsif text =~ RUB_FULL
        # "You are unable to add any more charges." means the item is full OR the orb isn't
        # valuable enough (gswiki). Short of the target, it's the orb: 2026-10-20 a 3,648 pink
        # sapphire orb stopped a golden wand at 17/40 and a drake wand at 17/34, while a 7,612
        # emerald orb took two drake wands to 35. That kind gets another go on the next orb.
        if rec[:charges] < rec[:target]
          rec[:status] = :orb_limit
          rec[:capped_orb] = @orb_count
          msg "#{rec[:name]} hit this orb's limit at #{rec[:charges]}/#{rec[:target]}#{rec[:retried] ? '' : '; it gets another try on the next orb'}."
        else
          rec[:status] = :full
        end
        break
      elsif text =~ RUB_FLOWS
        rec[:rubs] += 1
        msg "Couldn't channel the flows into the #{rec[:name]} (rub #{rec[:rubs]})."
      elsif text =~ RUB_NO_MANA
        if short_on_mana || mana_before >= (maxmana * RUB_MANA_SHARE).floor
          msg "Not enough mana to add a charge to the #{rec[:name]} even with #{mana_before}. Moving on."
          rec[:status] = :no_mana
          break
        end
        short_on_mana = true
      elsif text =~ RUB_NOT_READY
        @orb_ready = false
      elsif text =~ RUB_GONE
        @orb_id = nil
      else
        msg "Didn't recognize the response to RUB. The game said:"
        lines.each { |line| respond "    #{line}" }
        rec[:status] = :unknown
        break
      end
    end

    rec[:status] = :charged if rec[:status] == :partial && rec[:charges] >= rec[:target]
    dest = destination(rec)
    rec[:loc] = dest if stash(rec[:id], dest)
    # A greened item needs a fresh 405 next time; anything else keeps its new charge count
    if rec[:status] == :greened
      @survey_cache.delete(rec[:id].to_s)
    else
      cache_record(rec)
    end
    save_survey
    :done
  end

  # An item that hit an orb's limit gets one more try, on a later orb, if it has rubs left
  def self.retryable?(rec)
    rec[:status] == :orb_limit && !rec[:retried] && rec[:rubs] < max_rubs
  end

  def self.requeue(recs, queue)
    recs.each do |rec|
      @capped.delete(rec)
      queue << rec
    end
  end

  # Charges everything in order. An item stopped by the orb's limit is set aside and goes
  # back in line as soon as a newer orb exists. If some are still waiting when the line is
  # empty and there's a gem left, let this orb run out (it isn't re-prepped), then make
  # the next one for them.
  def self.charge_all(recs)
    queue = recs.dup
    waited = false
    loop do
      until queue.empty?
        rec = queue.shift
        # Marked when the retry really starts, so the report never claims one that didn't happen
        rec[:retried] = true if rec[:status] == :orb_limit
        result = charge(rec)
        result = charge(rec) while result == :orb_lost
        return if result == :stop

        @capped << rec if rec[:status] == :orb_limit && !@capped.include?(rec)
        requeue(@capped.select { |capped| retryable?(capped) && capped[:capped_orb] < @orb_count }, queue)
      end

      waiting = @capped.select { |capped| retryable?(capped) }
      return if waiting.empty? || waited
      if next_gem.nil?
        msg "No orb gems left to retry #{waiting.map { |capped| "the #{capped[:name]}" }.join(', ')} on another orb."
        return
      end
      waited = true
      return unless wait_out_orb(waiting)

      requeue(waiting, queue)
    end
  end

  # The orb can't add more to these, and a new orb can only be made once this one's gone
  ORB_WAIT_MAX = 30 * 60

  def self.wait_out_orb(waiting)
    names = waiting.map { |rec| "#{rec[:name]} (#{rec[:charges]}/#{rec[:target]})" }.join(', ')
    msg "Letting this orb run out so the next one can retry #{names}. Up to #{ORB_WAIT_MAX / 60} minutes; ;kill to stop here."
    started = Time.now
    reported = started
    while orb_alive?
      drain
      if Time.now - started > ORB_WAIT_MAX
        msg "The orb is still going after #{ORB_WAIT_MAX / 60} minutes. Leaving the retries for next time (--topoff)."
        return false
      end
      if Time.now - reported >= 5 * 60
        reported = Time.now
        msg "Still waiting for the orb to run out (#{((Time.now - started) / 60).floor} minutes so far)."
      end
      sleep 1
    end
    msg "The orb's gone. Making the next one for the retries."
    @orb_id = nil
    true
  end

  def self.destination(rec)
    return @greensack if rec[:status] == :greened && @greensack
    # A wand that didn't take a charge stays with the dead ones
    return rec[:src] if rec[:charges].to_i.zero?

    rec[:dst]
  end

  def self.go_to_workshop
    room = Room.current
    target = room&.find_nearest_by_tag(WORKSHOP_TAG)
    if target.nil?
      msg "Couldn't find a path to a Wizard Guild workshop. Charging here."
      return
    end
    return if room.id == target

    go2(target)
    msg "Didn't make it to the workshop (room #{target}). Charging here." unless Room.current&.id == target
  end

  # === report ====================================================================
  STATUS_TEXT = {
    charge: 'needs charging',
    partial: 'partly charged',
    charged: 'charged',
    full: "charged (can't add more)",
    orb_limit: 'orb limit (a more valuable orb may add more)',
    at_max: 'already at your max',
    greened: 'GREENED',
    no_mana: 'not enough mana',
    unknown: 'stopped (unrecognized response)',
    not_rechargeable: 'not mage rechargeable or empowerable',
    merchant: 'merchant rechargeable only',
    missing: "couldn't pick it up",
  }.freeze

  def self.report
    return if @reported || @records.empty?

    @reported = true
    respond
    msg "Report#{@gems_used.positive? ? " (#{@gems_used} orb gem#{@gems_used == 1 ? '' : 's'} used)" : ''}:"
    @records.each do |rec|
      spell = rec[:spell] ? " (#{rec[:spell]})" : ''
      charges = if !rec[:mage]
                  ''
                elsif rec[:before] == rec[:charges]
                  "  #{rec[:charges]}/#{rec[:target]} charges"
                else
                  "  #{rec[:before]} -> #{rec[:charges]}/#{rec[:target]} charges"
                end
      rubs = rec[:rubs].positive? ? ", #{rec[:rubs]} rub#{rec[:rubs] == 1 ? '' : 's'}" : ''
      rubs += ', retried on a second orb' if rec[:retried]
      respond "    #{rec[:name]}#{spell}#{charges}  #{STATUS_TEXT[rec[:status]] || rec[:status]}#{rubs}"
      respond "        #{rec[:wear]}" if rec[:wear] && rec[:mage] && rec[:wear] !~ WEAR_FINE
      rec[:raw].to_a.each { |line| respond "        | #{line}" }
    end
    respond
  end

  def self.help
    respond
    respond "charge_me_up_scotty - recharges spent wands and used magic items with Charge Item (517)."
    respond
    respond "Usage:"
    respond "  ;charge_me_up_scotty          survey with 405, then charge everything that needs it"
    respond "  ;charge_me_up_scotty check    survey only (no orb, no travel)"
    respond "  ;charge_me_up_scotty help     this help"
    respond
    respond "Options:"
    respond "  --here       charge where you are: no gem shop or workshop trip"
    respond "  --topoff     also top off fresh-container wands that are below your max"
    respond "  --fresh      cast 405 at everything again instead of using the last check"
    respond
    respond "Remembered between runs: 405 results (24 hours; a check refreshes them),"
    respond "gem appraisals (#{@gem_values.to_h.size rescue 0} gems), and poured gems not yet made into an orb."
    respond
    respond "Settings:"
    respond "  orbgemsack       #{setting(:orbgemsack) || '(not set)'}   orb gems (required to charge)"
    respond "  grotsack         #{setting(:grotsack) || "(orbgemsack)"}   grot t'kel potion (bought at the alchemist if there isn't one)"
    respond "  charge_pour      #{pour?}   pour grot t'kel on each gem first (false if they're pre-poured)"
    respond "  chargesack       #{setting(:chargesack) || '(not set)'}   used magic items to recharge"
    respond "  chargedsack      #{setting(:chargedsack) || '(chargesack)'}   recharged magic items"
    respond "  greensack        #{setting(:greensack) || '(not set)'}   greened items"
    respond "  charge_maxrubs   #{max_rubs}   most rubs per item per session"
    respond "  charge_symbol    #{symbol?}   use Voln's Symbol of Mana while waiting to rub (costs favor)"
    respond "  dead wands       #{op_setting('dead_wand_container', 'bag')}   from bigshot (dead_wand_container)"
    respond "  fresh wands      #{op_setting('fresh_wand_container', 'sack')}   from bigshot (fresh_wand_container)"
    respond
    respond "  Set with ;vars set <setting>=<value>, e.g. ;vars set orbgemsack=pouch"
    respond
  end

  # === main ======================================================================
  def self.run(args)
    # Module state survives between runs (Lich re-opens the module), so reset it
    @held = {}
    @records = []
    @bad_gems = []
    @orb_id = nil
    @orb_ready = false
    @gems_used = 0
    @orb_count = 0
    @capped = []
    @reported = false
    @cleaned_up = false
    @emptied_hands = false
    @symbol_off = false
    @survey_cache = recall('charge_survey', {})
    @gem_values = recall('charge_gem_values', {})
    @poured = recall('charge_poured', [])

    words = args.reject { |arg| arg.start_with?('--') }.map(&:downcase)
    here = args.include?('--here')
    @topoff = args.include?('--topoff')
    @fresh = args.include?('--fresh')

    if words.first =~ /^(help|\?)$/
      help
      exit
    end
    unless Spell[517].known? && Spell[405].known?
      msg "You need both Charge Item (517) and Elemental Detection (405)."
      exit
    end
    check_only = words.first == 'check'
    # A check is the explicit "look again", so it always casts 405 (and saves the results)
    @fresh ||= check_only

    unless check_only
      @gemsack = find_container(setting(:orbgemsack))
      @grotsack = find_container(setting(:grotsack)) || @gemsack
      @greensack = find_container(setting(:greensack))
      if @gemsack.nil?
        msg(setting(:orbgemsack) ? "Can't find your orbgemsack (#{setting(:orbgemsack)})." : "Set where your orb gems are first: ;vars set orbgemsack=<container>")
        exit
      end
    end

    # before_dying, not ensure: on ;kill the script's thread dies first and fput from
    # its ensure fails; before_dying runs after, where fput still works
    before_dying { ChargeMeUpScotty.cleanup }
    # A gem poured on a run that stopped before the orb was made goes back with the orb
    # gems instead of wherever empty_hands would stash it
    if @gemsack
      %w[right left].each { |side|
        next unless hand(side).id && @poured.include?(hand(side).id.to_s)

        msg "Putting the poured #{hand(side).name} back in your #{@gemsack.name}; it'll be the next orb."
        stash_hand(side, @gemsack)
      }
    end
    empty_hands
    @emptied_hands = true

    survey
    to_charge = @records.select { |rec| rec[:status] == :charge }
    if check_only || to_charge.empty?
      msg "Nothing needs charging." if to_charge.empty? && !@records.empty?
      return
    end

    # Gems, appraisals and potion before the workshop, so none of those trips start from it
    start_room = Room.current&.id
    if next_gem.nil? && orb_ids.empty?
      msg "No orb gems in your #{@gemsack.name}. Stopping."
      return
    end
    appraise_gems unless here
    first_gem = next_gem
    if pour? && first_gem && !poured?(first_gem) && ensure_potion.nil?
      msg "No grot t'kel potion to pour on your orb gems. Stopping."
      return
    end

    go_to_workshop unless here
    adopt_orb unless orb_ids.empty?

    charge_all(to_charge)
    msg "The pulsating orb is still here if you have more to charge." if orb_alive?

    go2(start_room) if start_room && !here && Room.current&.id != start_room
  end

  # Puts back anything we took out, re-equips what was in hand, prints the report
  def self.cleanup
    return if @cleaned_up

    @cleaned_up = true
    fput "release" unless checkprep == 'None'
    @held.to_a.each { |id, from| fput "put ##{id} in ##{from.id}" if held?(id) }
    fill_hands if @emptied_hands
    report
  end
end

ChargeMeUpScotty.run(Script.current.vars[1..] || [])
